---
const steps = [
  {
    title: "Your file opens in this tab",
    body: "You pick a file. Your browser reads it straight from your disk. Nothing is sent anywhere.",
    sticky: "bg-sticky-yellow",
  },
  {
    title: "The engine runs on your device",
    body: "A PDF engine compiled to WebAssembly does the work inside your browser, in a background thread.",
    sticky: "bg-sticky-lavender",
  },
  {
    title: "You save the result",
    body: "The finished PDF is handed back to you as a download. No queue, no account, no watermark.",
    sticky: "bg-sticky-mint",
  },
];
---

<section id="how-it-works" class="scroll-mt-20 px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 md:py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl">How it works without uploading</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-muted">
        Other sites send your document to a server and back. Plyleaf brings the software to your document instead.
        That's why it's private, and why it can stay free.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      {steps.map(({ title, body, sticky }, i) => (
        <li class="relative rounded-card border border-line bg-surface p-6">
          <span
            class:list={[
              "grid size-12 -rotate-6 place-items-center rounded-lg font-display text-2xl font-extrabold shadow-sticky",
              sticky,
            ]}
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            {i + 1}
          </span>
          <h3 class="mt-5 text-2xl">{title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">{body}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <div class="mt-8 flex items-center gap-4 rounded-card border-2 border-dashed border-line p-5 text-ink-muted">
      <svg
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        class="size-8 shrink-0"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="2"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <path d="M7 18a4.5 4.5 0 0 1-.6-9A6 6 0 0 1 18 8a4 4 0 0 1 0 8M3 3l18 18" />
      </svg>
      <p>
        <strong class="text-ink">No server in between.</strong> The code is open source, so anyone can check that your
        files never leave your device.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
